1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:02,720
This diver was searching for dead bodies...

2
00:00:03,090 --> 00:00:04,820
when someone grabbed his hand.

3
00:00:05,320 --> 00:00:07,430
The man was Harrison Okene.

4
00:00:07,530 --> 00:00:09,180
His ship had already been underwater

5
00:00:09,200 --> 00:00:11,050
for nearly 60 hours.

6
00:00:11,600 --> 00:00:15,080
Back in 2013, the tugboat Jascon-4 capsized

7
00:00:15,100 --> 00:00:16,620
off the coast of Nigeria.

8
00:00:17,070 --> 00:00:18,680
As the vessel filled with water,

9
00:00:18,700 --> 00:00:20,420
Harrison made it into a small trapped

10
00:00:20,440 --> 00:00:22,100
air pocket inside the wreck.

11
00:00:22,300 --> 00:00:23,940
And that air pocket is the reason he

12
00:00:23,960 --> 00:00:25,540
didn't die immediately.

13
00:00:25,840 --> 00:00:27,210
Here's the important part:

14
00:00:27,340 --> 00:00:29,060
a trapped pocket of air can keep someone

15
00:00:29,080 --> 00:00:30,200
alive for a while...

16
00:00:30,220 --> 00:00:31,760
but only temporarily.

17
00:00:31,960 --> 00:00:33,410
Oxygen gets used up.

18
00:00:33,430 --> 00:00:35,150
Carbon dioxide builds up.

19
00:00:35,200 --> 00:00:36,970
And the safe space can shrink as water

20
00:00:36,990 --> 00:00:37,810
rises.

21
00:00:38,260 --> 00:00:40,240
So every hour inside that wreck made

22
00:00:40,260 --> 00:00:41,680
survival less likely.

23
00:00:42,430 --> 00:00:43,950
He waited there in darkness...

24
00:00:43,970 --> 00:00:45,640
until rescue divers finally entered

25
00:00:45,660 --> 00:00:46,390
the ship.

26
00:00:46,740 --> 00:00:48,800
They were expecting to recover bodies.

27
00:00:49,250 --> 00:00:50,060
Instead...

28
00:00:50,210 --> 00:00:51,540
they found a survivor.

29
00:00:52,190 --> 00:00:54,570
Harrison Okene had stayed alive underwater

30
00:00:54,590 --> 00:00:56,550
for nearly 60 hours.
